# Copy to .env and adjust. Do not put secrets in this file.
#
# There are two ways to reach a model — pick one. Every setting below is
# commented out because each path has a working default; uncomment only what
# you actually need to change.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Option A — through the interview proxy. No AWS account, no credentials.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Setting both AIET_PROXY_URL and AIET_TOKEN switches the agent onto the proxy
# automatically. The token is short-lived (1 hour) and is supplied to you
# separately — it does not belong in this file or in git. Export it instead:
#
#   export AIET_TOKEN=<the token you were given>
#
AIET_PROXY_URL=https://nbylnotlx5fcsdkawr3ntxfita0nhyrg.lambda-url.us-west-2.on.aws/

# On the proxy, the model must be one of: sonnet-5, sonnet-4.5, haiku-4.5.
# Defaults to sonnet-4.5. The proxy also caps output at 4096 tokens, request
# bodies at 32 KB, and 10 requests per 60 seconds.
# AGENT_MODEL=sonnet-4.5

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Option B — straight to Bedrock with your own AWS credentials.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Used whenever AIET_TOKEN is unset. Credentials are NOT read from here —
# Bedrock uses the AWS SDK default provider chain (environment variables,
# AWS_PROFILE, SSO, or an instance role).
#
# Note the model ids differ between the two options: a Bedrock cross-region
# inference profile here, a short name on the proxy. Do not set one for the
# other path.
# AGENT_MODEL=us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929-v1:0

# Region to call Bedrock in. Falls back to AWS_REGION, then us-east-1.
# Ignored on the proxy, which always lives in us-west-2.
# AGENT_AWS_REGION=us-east-1
